#. translators: 1: opening link tag, 2: closing link tag.
#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:212
#, php-format
msgid "Image URLs on the front end are rewritten to %1$swsrv.nl%2$s, a free image proxy that resizes and re-encodes on the fly and serves the result from a CDN. Your own files are untouched, and turning this off puts every URL back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:219
msgid "The proxy fetches each image from your site, so it only works on a site that is reachable from the internet. On a local or password protected site the images will not load."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:229
msgid "Rewrite front end image URLs to the proxy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:244
msgid "WebP files are a good deal smaller than JPEG or PNG and every current browser reads them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:251
msgid "WordPress normally cuts every registered size the moment a file is uploaded, most of which no page ever asks for. With this on, an upload keeps only its own file and each size is cut the first time something requests it, then stays on disk like any other."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:254
msgid "Uploads get quicker and the uploads folder stays smaller. The first visitor to need a size waits for it to be cut, and until then an image has no other size to offer in its srcset."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:264
msgid "Cut each size when it is first requested, not on upload"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:266
msgid "Rebuilding from the Rebuild tab still generates whatever you select there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:278
msgid "This site has no image sizes registered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:289
msgid "A size ticked here is never written on upload and is skipped by a rebuild, whatever the Rebuild tab has selected. It is cut the first time a page asks for it. Useful for the big sizes only a handful of pages ever use."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:297
msgid "A WebP copy is written next to every image WordPress generates, and the front end serves it through a picture element with the original as the fallback. Your JPEG and PNG files stay where they are, and a copy that would be larger than the original is thrown away."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: opening link tag to the Rebuild tab, 2: closing link tag.
#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:303
#, php-format
msgid "New uploads are converted as they arrive. For the images already in the library, %1$srun a rebuild%2$s once after turning this on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:311
msgid "The image library on this server cannot write WebP, so no copies will be made. Ask your host for GD or Imagick with WebP support."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:316
msgid "This works on its own, but the proxy above is on and already delivers WebP from its CDN for the images it rewrites. The copies made here are what gets served whenever the proxy is off or does not handle an image."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:327
msgid "Convert generated images to WebP and serve the copies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:336
msgid "1 to 100, used when writing the WebP copies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-atr-settings.php:344
msgid "1 to 100. Around 80 is the usual compromise between file size and artefacts."
msgstr ""

